Q: Embed PDF in mobile browsers A: <p>PDF.js is a good option. Consider using <a href="https://github.com/alekswebnet/pdfjs-viewer-element" rel="nofollow noreferrer">pdfjs-viewer-element</a> to embed the PDF viewer. This is a web component wraps PDF.js viewer and works in a simple HTML / with any JS framework just putting it on the page.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot; src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pdfjs-viewer-element/dist/pdfjs-viewer-element.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;pdfjs-viewer-element
  src=&quot;https://alekswebnet.github.io/sample-pdf-with-images.pdf&quot;
  style=&quot;height: 100dvh&quot;&gt;
&lt;/pdfjs-viewer-element&gt;
</code></pre>
